  "gold_with_text_not_included": [
   {
    "pmid": "15501593",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Task fMRI (I1) in 14 healthy girls (I4) instructed to reappraise by distancing (I2) during sad and neutral film excerpts (I3), with main effects and emotion x regulation interaction contrasts (I5). However, all reported peaks (text and Table 1) carry small-volume-corrected P values within a priori ROIs (LPFC, MPFC, OFC, ACC, VLPFC, temporal pole, midbrain). The text states a whole-brain search was carried out but reports no whole-brain results, so a whole-brain voxelwise map with coordinates was not demonstrated (I6 not met). E2 left unclear because a whole-brain search is claimed but not reported."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "17488204",
    "decision": "incomplete",
    "failed": [],
    "autonima": "fulltext_incomplete",
    "reason": "The text file is a publisher landing page with only the abstract; it states the content is only available as a PDF. There are no Methods, Results or tables, so I4-I6 and E2-E4 cannot be judged. The abstract indicates event-related fMRI with increase/decrease regulation of emotional reactions to pictures (I1-I3). Return to retrieval."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "19555702",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Task fMRI (I1) in healthy young adults (I4). Participants were told to reduce negative or positive emotion versus simply view (I2) IAPS and media pictures (I3). The regulate > view contrasts are defined (I5). However, the only coordinate table (Table 1) gives between-sex ANOVA F-maxima in a priori prefrontal and limbic regions, with within-group post hoc t tests on peak-voxel signal change. No group-level whole-brain within-task map with peak coordinates is reported, even though whole-brain analyses are mentioned, so I6 was not demonstrated. E2 and E4 are unclear because of the a priori region thresholding and the between-sex focus."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "21712804",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Task fMRI (I1) in 17 healthy women (I4) viewing food pictures (I3), with a whole-brain REGULATE_TASTY vs ADMIT_TASTY contrast in MNI space (I5, I6). However, the regulated state is appetitive desire/craving for food, not an emotional response; the paper itself distinguishes reinterpretation as an emotion regulation strategy from its application to craving and reward. The task is regulation of food desire rather than an instructed emotion regulation strategy toward an emotional response, so I2 is not demonstrated (not_met). Borderline case: craving regulation."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "21907809",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3"
    ],
    "autonima": "excluded_fulltext",
    "reason": "Reappraisal (distancing/enhance vs maintain) fMRI study in BPD, trauma-exposed and healthy women, with whole-brain one-sample tests per group (Table S3, MNI). However, the regulated emotional stimuli are verbal first-person narrative scripts (ANET) of 3-4 sentences, i.e. sentence stimuli, not visual images or film, so I3 is not met."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "22613776",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6",
     "E2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "fMRI study of reappraisal and distraction of IAPS pictures in remitted MDD and healthy controls, with one-sample within-group tests for each group (I1-I5 met). However, all analyses were restricted to anatomically defined ROIs (amygdala, OFC, dlPFC, dmPFC, ACC, parietal) with FWE correction; no whole-brain voxelwise analysis is reported, so E2 is met and I6 not met."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "24782800",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6",
     "E2"
    ],
    "autonima": "excluded_fulltext",
    "reason": "Task fMRI in younger and older adults reappraising (detached/positive reappraisal) or using selective attention vs passive viewing of negative film clips, with within-group regulation > view contrasts (I1-I5 met). However, all contrasts were restricted by an explicit mask covering only PFC, ACC and amygdala; no whole-brain voxelwise analysis is reported (I6 not met, E2 met)."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "25461265",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6",
     "E2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Real-time fMRI neurofeedback study with cognitive reappraisal of IAPS aversive images in healthy adults (I1-I4 met); group reappraisal > view contrast reported in Talairach coordinates (I5). However, acquisition used 26 slices giving only partial brain coverage, with limited coverage of high parietal cortex and cerebellum, so no true whole-brain map exists (E2 met, I6 not met), despite the authors labelling the analysis whole-brain. Close call on coverage."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "25617820",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6",
     "E2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Task fMRI with instructed acceptance and reappraisal of sad IAPS images (I1-I3 met); within-group control results (accept > view, accept > reappraise) reported in MNI tables (I4, I5 met). However, all analyses were thresholded within an a priori small-volume mask of the frontal lobes and bilateral amygdala, and all reported clusters are frontal/insular; no unmasked whole-brain map is reported (E2 met, I6 not met)."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "26529426",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I4"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Task fMRI (I1) with instructed cognitive reappraisal vs Maintain (I2) of negative IAPS images (I3); whole-brain MNI peaks for Reappraisal vs Maintain (I5, I6). However, the sample is panic disorder patients plus controls, and the within-task whole-brain effect is reported only pooled across both groups; other whole-brain results are patient-vs-control contrasts. The control group's results are never reported separately, so I4 (clinical study qualifies only when control results are reported separately) is not met."
   }
  ]
